---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// Welcome to Astro! Wondering what to do next? Check out the Astro documentation at https://docs.astro.build
// Don't want to use any of this? Delete everything in this file, the `assets`, `components`, and `layouts` directories, and start fresh.
---

<Layout>
  <Header />
  <main class="about-content">
    <section class="container py-4 policy-document">
        <h1>Donation Policy</h1>

        <p>
          <strong>Voice of Ex-Servicemen</strong> is committed to maintaining transparency
          and accountability in the receipt and utilisation of donations. This Donation
          Policy explains the terms and conditions applicable to donations made through
          our website.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Acceptance of Donations</h2>

        <p>
          Voice of Ex-Servicemen accepts voluntary donations from individuals
          and organisations through the payment methods made available on our
          website. Donations are intended to support the organisation's
          activities, welfare initiatives, awareness programmes, administrative
          requirements, and other legitimate objectives of the organisation.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Voluntary Contribution</h2>

        <p>
          All donations made through this website are voluntary contributions. A
          donor should make a donation only after carefully reviewing the amount
          and payment details before completing the transaction.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Online Payment</h2>

        <p>
          Online donations may be processed through third-party payment gateway
          providers. Voice of Ex-Servicemen does not directly store or have
          access to sensitive payment information such as debit card numbers,
          credit card numbers, CVV, UPI PINs, or internet banking passwords.
        </p>

        <p>
          Donors are required to provide accurate information during the
          donation process. The processing of payments is subject to the terms
          and policies of the applicable payment gateway and the donor's bank or
          financial institution.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Donation Confirmation</h2>

        <p>
          Once a successful donation transaction is received and confirmed by
          the payment gateway, a confirmation or acknowledgement may be provided
          to the donor through the email address or other contact information
          submitted during the donation process.
        </p>

        <p>
          A payment transaction shown as successful by a bank or payment service
          does not necessarily mean that the donation has been received by the
          organisation. The donation will be considered received only after
          confirmation of the transaction by the applicable payment system or
          our records.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Failed or Incomplete Transactions</h2>

        <p>
          If an online donation transaction fails, is cancelled, or remains
          incomplete, no donation will be considered successfully received
          unless the amount is subsequently credited to the organisation's
          account.
        </p>

        <p>
          In cases where the donor's account has been debited but the donation
          has not been credited to the organisation, the donor should contact us
          with the relevant transaction details so that the matter can be
          verified.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Refund and Cancellation Policy</h2>

        <p>
          Donations made voluntarily through this website are generally
          <strong>non-refundable and cannot be cancelled</strong> once the transaction
          has been successfully completed.
        </p>

        <p>
          However, if a donation has been made due to a genuine technical error,
          duplicate transaction, or other exceptional circumstance, the donor
          may contact us within a reasonable period with the transaction
          details. Any refund request will be reviewed and processed at the sole
          discretion of the organisation, subject to verification and applicable
          payment gateway and banking procedures.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Duplicate Payments</h2>

        <p>
          If a donor believes that the same donation has been charged more than
          once, the donor should contact us as soon as possible with the
          transaction reference numbers and other relevant details. Duplicate
          transactions will be verified before any eligible refund is
          considered.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Use of Donations</h2>

        <p>
          Donations received by Voice of Ex-Servicemen may be utilised for
          activities consistent with the aims and objectives of the
          organisation. These may include Ex-Servicemen welfare activities,
          awareness programmes, advocacy, assistance initiatives, organisational
          activities, and reasonable administrative and operational expenses.
        </p>

        <p>
          Unless a specific purpose is expressly stated and accepted by the
          organisation, donations may be allocated according to the
          organisation's current priorities and requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Donor Information</h2>

        <p>
          We respect the privacy of our donors. Personal information collected
          during the donation process will be handled in accordance with our
          <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Donors should not submit sensitive payment credentials, including card
          PINs, UPI PINs, passwords, or similar confidential information to us
          through email, forms, or other communication channels.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Tax Benefits and Donation Receipts</h2>

        <p>
          Where applicable, donation receipts or other documentation may be
          issued in accordance with applicable laws and the organisation's
          eligibility and registration status.
        </p>

        <p>
          Donors should ensure that the information provided during the donation
          process, including their name, address, email address, and other
          required details, is accurate if they require an official receipt or
          documentation.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Fraudulent or Unauthorised Transactions</h2>

        <p>
          Voice of Ex-Servicemen reserves the right to investigate transactions
          that appear to be fraudulent, unauthorised, suspicious, or
          inconsistent with applicable laws and regulations.
        </p>

        <p>
          Where necessary, suspicious transactions may be reported to the
          relevant payment service provider, bank, or competent authority.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>

        <p>
          Voice of Ex-Servicemen reserves the right to modify or update this
          Donation Policy from time to time. Any changes will be published on
          this page with the updated effective date.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Contact Us</h2>

        <p>
          If you have any questions regarding a donation, payment transaction,
          refund request, or this Donation Policy, please contact us using the
          contact information provided on our website.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Organisation:</strong> Voice of Ex-Servicemen<br />
          <strong>Website:</strong>
          <a href="https://www.voiceofexservicemen.in/">
            www.voiceofexservicemen.in
          </a>
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Effective Date:</strong> [Insert Date]
        </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
